The top three commonly used clouds
1. AWS ☁️
2. Microsoft Azure ☁️
3. Google Cloud ☁️

Each cloud provides services such as:

| Service      | Example                          |
| ------------ | -------------------------------- |
| 💻 Computing | Run applications                 |
| 📦 Storage   | Store files and data             |
| 🗄️ Database | Store application data           |
| 🤖 AI/ML     | Train and use AI models          |
| 🌐 Hosting   | Deploy websites and applications |
| 🔐 Security  | Protect applications and data    |


For your project

You are currently using Google Cloud:

Google Cloud Platform
│
├── Cloud Shell → Write/run cloud commands
├── Vertex AI → AI and Gemini services
├── Cloud Run → Deploy your application
└── Docker → Package your application

So, think of cloud as renting powerful computers and services through the internet instead of buying and maintaining your own servers.

Your current College AI Assistant is a good example of a cloud-based AI application because it uses Google Cloud services for deployment and AI.

Cloud computing is not one single cloud; it is a category of internet-based services, and 
the main cloud deployment types are public, private, hybrid, and multicloud.

